 "REFLECTION": {
  "status": "COMPLETE",
  "1_passfail_and_decision": "CONFIRMATORY: preflight 9/9 PASS (qk_reconstruction, stage7_equals_clean, positionwise_reconstruction all EXACT=0.0; reference_is_clean_sequence AG-intact; resolution_pair_match; real_acceptor_arm_available n_real=120; both strands; checkpoint). n=260, n_real=120, 230 genes. Decision table -> ROW 1: the targeting DIFFERENCE is pre-resident, not layer-constructed. S_J is ~fully present at the all-ref floor (primary +3.14 vs full +3.04; secondary +3.49 vs +3.54) and the reciprocal leave-one-out isolates the EMBEDDINGS as necessary (embed drop +3.19 primary / +3.08 secondary; every layer-0/1/2 stage |drop|<0.9, several negative). Next = token-vs-position 2x2 (prereg 5.1).",
  "2_sufficiency_not_computation": "The prefix denoising curve is ~FLAT with a mid-hump (floor +3.14 -> attn1 +3.77 -> full +3.04), so the difference is NOT accumulated across layers 0-2. Necessity (recompute LOO) and sufficiency (fixed-reference prefix) AGREE that the difference originates pre-layer-3 in the embeddings: referencing ONLY the embedding while layers recompute collapses S_J to -0.15, i.e. the attention/MLP layers do not independently construct the preference without the embedding signal. The two counterfactuals differ (recompute vs fixed suffix) and both are reported; neither shows a layer-localized constructor.",
  "3_key_query_interaction_and_classlift": "S_K (key provenance) rises monotonically +2.52->+3.04 (keys add ~+0.5). S_Q (query provenance) is HIGH at the generic floor (+3.74) and FALLS at layer 2 to +3.04 (the specific query reduces the DIFFERENCE). Per-curve attraction explains why: under the query config, reconstructing the donor query (largest jump at mlp2) raises BOTH a+ and the decoy vs background together (primary a+ +5.59->+7.42, decoy +1.41->+2.63; secondary a+ +5.41->+7.20, decoy +0.47->+1.53) -- a CLASS-LEVEL acceptor gain, invisible to a+-decoy. This RESOLVES C20: layer-2/L2H15 query construction contributes to COUPLING via absolute acceptor attraction (gain), not identity discrimination -- consistent with 66% of coupling but 11% of preference.",
  "4_S_A_is_intermediate_confounds": "S_A is a mechanistic intermediate; NO partner-selection behavioural claim is made. The PRIMARY (real-acceptor) arm has a large distance confound (signed gap median +19.5nt, abs mean 30.2), so its difference is substantially distance-decay. The SECONDARY (generic-AG, distance/phase matched) arm conflates identity with site-strength salience. A0 therefore localizes a geometry/salience-laden targeting difference to the embeddings and characterizes the query's class-lift; it does NOT establish partner identity. The withdrawn matched-decoy behavioural claim stays withdrawn.",
  "5_escaped_failure_modes": "(a) The all-ref floor ~= full (not zero) is the role-specific mean-resample design (prereg 3 amendment), reported not gated; it means the difference is carried by the generic role structure (position/distance/site-strength). (b) Endpoint identity S_K(7)=S_Q(7)=S_J(7) holds exactly (checked live). (c) The naive 'embeddings are everything' reading is guarded against: embed-ref-only=-0.15 vs all-ref=+3.14 is an interaction (recompute vs fixed), so the honest claim is embedding-RESIDENT difference + layer conduit + query class-gain, not 'embeddings construct it in isolation'. (d) The primary-arm distance confound blocks any identity claim.",
  "overall": "The diffuse-builder hypothesis (C20's tempting read) is RETIRED. L3H1's targeting DIFFERENCE is pre-resident in the token+positional embeddings (position/distance + local site content), not constructed by layers 0-2. The upstream query pathway (peaking at mlp2/L2H15) instead supplies CLASS-LEVEL acceptor attraction gain, which resolves the coupling-vs-preference discrepancy. A1 should NOT run a builder scan; route to (i) the token-vs-position 2x2 to split the embedding-resident difference into geometry vs content, and (ii) a focused test of the mlp2/L2H15 query-gain -> coupling link."
 }
